    "rules": [
      "Apply only to the exact logical-table-definition and physical-table-definition canonical kinds. Preserve their existing spec-meta sheet contract, two canonical HEADER and detail LIST chapters, exact column headers and all existing validation requirements.",
      "Within each HEADER and detail LIST chapter, emit only its required Markdown table and surrounding blank lines. Do not append h3 headings, paragraphs, numbered or bulleted procedures, code fences, SQL fences, Mermaid diagrams or other out-of-table body blocks. Keep the HEADER as its single two-column table and the detail list as its prescribed table.",
      "Preserve every source-supported valid fact, condition, branch, exception, constraint, use and evidence location already relevant to this table definition inside the appropriate table cells. Inline code, concise labels and permitted line breaks may organize cells. Do not fix format by omitting supported facts, adding facts, claiming runtime proof or assembling business prose outside the AI response.",
      "Where detailed process or diagram responsibility belongs to an existing planned GRID document, cite only a source-supported responsibility and exact existing plan document ID and relative path in the related-document table cells. A planned responsibility is not proof that the other document has been generated, reviewed or already contains the explanation. Preserve the relevant facts in this table and state the reference as planned or unverified unless pinned current-run evidence proves its state; do not create or alter that other document from this task.",
      "Return the complete source-backed Markdown, not a patch. Preserve full execution context, exact source-only boundaries, observed-source basis, whole preserved previous Markdown and review when provided, official completed-analysis reuse truth, fresh AI drafting and independent review. Pure format metadata supplies neither business facts nor additional read authority."
    ]
  },
